<title>USA: Angeion adds tachycardia expert.</title>
<headline>Angeion adds tachycardia expert.</headline>
<dateline>MINNEAPOLIS 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Angeion Corp said on Thursday that Michael Kallok, an expert on tachycardia, or too rapid, abnormal heart beat, has joined the company as vice president of research.</p>
<p>He will direct the company's research, intellectual property activities and concept development of Angeion's line of implantable cardioverter defibrillators.</p>
<p>Angeion president Whitney McFarlin said Kallok &quot;is considered by industry leaders as one of the top tachyarrhythmia experts in the world.&quot;</p>
<p>Angeion said Kallok has had 17 years of research and management experience in biomaterials research, heart valves and tachyarrhythmia. From 1988 to 1995 he held a variety of positions at Medtronic Inc.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
